    .Description = "Medium tank of the Red Army, with sloped armor, a powerful gun and wide tracks for mud and snow. Designed to defeat infantry and ranged units, but vulnerable to anti-cavalry units.", 
    .EncartaStrategy = "Tank unique to the Soviet Union, stronger than the other tanks of its era. Use it to break enemy infantry lines and keep it away from anti-cavalry units.", 
    .EncartaHistory = "The T-34 entered service in 1940 and became the symbol of the Soviet war effort. Its sloped armor, 76 mm gun and wide tracks surprised the German army in 1941, and its simple design allowed factories evacuated to the Urals, such as the \xE2\x80\x9CTankograd\xE2\x80\x9D complex in Chelyabinsk, to build more than 80,000 of them during the war. T-34s fought at Moscow, Stalingrad and in the great tank battle of Kursk, and in 1945 they rolled into Berlin.", 
